    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d527">

                <pb facs="0579" n="565" sameAs="frus:frus1944v07/pg565"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">711.3227/131a: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Ambassador in Brazil</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Caffery</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1944-06-23T21:00:00-04:00">June 23, 1944—9
                            p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1928. The Department is issuing an invitation to the Brazilian Government through
                    the Embassy here to hold bilateral exploratory conversations for the purpose of
                    exchanging views on post-war aviation, with particular reference to the
                    development of international air transport. During these conversations we plan
                    to submit a draft of <pb facs="0580" n="566" xml:id="pg566"/> a proposed
                    bilateral agreement on international air transport for the study and comments of
                    the Brazilian Government.</p>
                <p>Accordingly, the Department believes that unless you have already commenced
                    negotiations, you should not now submit the draft civil aviation agreement which
                    was forwarded to you with the Department’s instruction 5691, March 2,
                        1944.<anchor n="51" xml:id="d527-f1"/>
                </p>
                <p>Because of the special situation existing in regard to airports in Brazil, there
                    will be included in the draft air transport agreement<anchor n="52"
                        xml:id="d527-f2"/> an article similar to Article 22 of the draft agreement
                    sent to you on March 2d.<anchor n="53" xml:id="d527-f3"/>
                </p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d527-f1" n="51" xml:id="d527-f1-content">
                <p>Not printed.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d527-f2" n="52" xml:id="d527-f2-content">
                <p>Discussion of this proposed agreement appears to have been indefinitely deferred
                    in favor of proposed multilateral conventions on air navigation and air
                    transport. For correspondence on these general agreements, see <ref
                        target="frus1944v02#pg_355">vol. <hi rendition="#small-caps">ii</hi>, pp.
                        355</ref> ff.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d527-f3" n="53" xml:id="d527-f3-content">
                <p>Draft agreement of March 2 not printed.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
